    "description": "The merchant checkout application has a PaymentScreen implemented with the company UI framework. The framework constructs this screen, supplies its window, and invokes callbacks for field changes and the Pay button. The screen currently decides whether the card number, billing address, and purchase limit are acceptable, and it decides whether the user may advance to confirmation. Unit tests cannot construct PaymentScreen without starting a window server and dispatching framework events, so these rules are checked only through a slow browser suite. The required change is to make every checkout eligibility decision verifiable in a fast, synchronous test while preserving the framework behavior that renders fields, forwards user events, and starts navigation. The team must choose where the eligibility and progression rules should reside without changing the externally visible checkout flow, adding network calls to the fast tests, or duplicating the rules between the screen and the tests.",
    "decision_statement": "Decide where the payment validation and navigation rules should live so they can be verified synchronously outside the framework-controlled screen.",
    "notes": "Humble-object fits because the framework constructs PaymentScreen and the eligibility rules move to a synchronously testable collaborator while the screen keeps rendering and event forwarding; test-specific-subclass is the only same-family sibling and a plausible alternative seam."
  },
